<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-12">12 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Reagan urges Gorbachev to 'tear down this wall'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Speaking at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> Gate, President Reagan challenged the Soviet leader to open the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a>. It fell two and a half years later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-19">19 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Black Monday: stock markets crash worldwide</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 508 points, or 22.6 per cent, its largest one-day percentage fall. Markets crashed worldwide, though the wider economy recovered far faster than after 1929.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/sino-portuguese-joint-declaration">Sino-Portuguese Joint Declaration</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Sino-Portuguese Joint Declaration was signed in Beijing on 13 April 1987 by Portugal and the People's Republic of China.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/esquipulas-peace-agreement">Esquipulas Peace Agreement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Esquipulas Peace Agreement, or Esquipulas II, was signed on 7 August 1987 in Guatemala City by the presidents of Guatemala, El Salvador, Honduras, Nicaragua and Costa Rica, following a first summit at Esquipulas in Guatemala in 1986.</p></div></li></ol></section>
